EXPERIMENT 2 - OPEN MP MATRIX MULTIPLICATION 
# Experiment 2: OpenMP Matrix Multiplication

## Objective

To implement and execute parallel matrix multiplication using OpenMP and measure the execution time using multiple CPU threads.

## Description

In this experiment, two 4000 × 4000 matrices are initialized with the value 1.0. Matrix multiplication is performed using OpenMP to parallelize the computation across multiple CPU threads.

The outer loop of the matrix multiplication is divided among OpenMP threads so that multiple portions of the computation can be performed simultaneously.

The resulting matrix is:

C = A × B

Since all elements of matrices A and B are 1.0, the expected value of C[0][0] is 4000.00.

## Compilation

The OpenMP program was compiled using GCC with OpenMP support:

```bash
gcc -O2 -fopenmp openmp.c -o open


##Result##

The OpenMP matrix multiplication was successfully completed.

Matrix Size: 4000 × 4000
Number of Threads Used: 16
Execution Time: 119.906317 seconds
Verification C[0][0]: 4000.00

Conclusion

The OpenMP matrix multiplication program was successfully compiled and executed using 16 CPU threads. The verification value C[0][0] = 4000.00 confirms that the expected matrix multiplication result was obtained.
